{"id":54095,"ord":82,"n_segments":112,"prev":54094,"next":54096,"doc":{"id":"67750","title":"67750_Sippie Wallace oral history interview","collection":"rutgers","inst":"Rutgers — Institute of Jazz Studies","interviewee":"Sippie Wallace","interviewer":"","date":"","year":"","source_url":"https://rucore.libraries.rutgers.edu/rutgers-lib/67750/","url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=67750"},"chapter":"Songs, Spivey and Europe 1966","title":"Who played on Hocile's records","category":"recording_session","summary":"They correct the personnel on Hocile's recordings, with Herschel and Buddy Christian.","period":"1920s","year_from":1920,"year_to":1929,"words":125,"start":[140,2],"end":[141,5],"url":"https://thisismattmiller.github.io/linked-jazz-2026-transcripts/?t=67750#s54095","tags":{"places":[],"venues":[],"bands":[]},"people":[{"name":"Hociel Thomas","qid":"Q1622571","n":2},{"name":"Buddy Christian","qid":"Q2927519","n":1},{"name":"Hersal Thomas","qid":"Q1614502","n":1}],"story":{"theme":34,"theme_name":"Who was in the band: naming sidemen and personnel","community":60,"community_name":"Who played in the band: reciting personnel","core":false},"blocks":[{"p":140,"b":2,"s":"MS. REITZ","x":"You said that was Buddy Christian playing the banjo on that tune \"You're Going to Need My Help\" that Hocile was singing."},{"p":140,"b":3,"s":"MS. WALLACE","x":"Uh-huh. Who did you say it was?"},{"p":140,"b":4,"s":"MS. REITZ","x":"They don't have that down right at all. They don't have that right at all here. And that was Hocile playing the piano too, you said?"},{"p":140,"b":5,"s":"MS. WALLACE","x":"?"},{"p":140,"b":6,"s":"MS. REITZ","x":"On \"You're Going to Need My Help,\" that tune that we played."},{"p":140,"b":7,"s":"MS. WALLACE","x":"Uh-huh. \"Go Down, Sunshine.\""},{"p":140,"b":8,"s":"MS. REITZ","x":"What?"},{"p":140,"b":9,"s":"MS. WALLACE","x":"\"Go Down, Sunshine.\""},{"p":140,"b":10,"s":"MS. REITZ","x":"\"Go Down, Sunshine Blues?\""},{"p":140,"b":11,"s":"MS. WALLACE","x":"Uh-huh."},{"p":140,"b":12,"s":"MS. REITZ","x":"She played the piano on that?"},{"p":140,"b":13,"s":"MS. WALLACE","x":"Yeah, uh-huh."},{"p":140,"b":14,"s":"MS. REITZ","x":"Well, we had those others, too, the \"Dead"},{"p":141,"b":0,"s":"MS. REITZ","x":"Drunk Blues,\" \"Have You Ever Been Drunk?\", and \"Lazy Man Blues.\""},{"p":141,"b":1,"s":"MS. WALLACE","x":"(Unintelligible) played them."},{"p":141,"b":2,"s":"MS. REITZ","x":"What? Herschel played on those, yeah."},{"p":141,"b":3,"s":"MS. WALLACE","x":"(Unintelligible)."},{"p":141,"b":4,"s":"MS. REITZ","x":"Okay, well, --"},{"p":141,"b":5,"s":"","x":"(End of Side Five.)"}]}